-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  cpp_expression.pcpp - C++ integration compliance: cpp("...")

  cpp("...") is a C++ expression written as a plain string (BNF.md sec 10),
  emitted in place; a raw string, cpp(R"(...)"), may span lines and hold
  quotes unescaped.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_expression.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_expression.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    abs 5
    raw 3
    lines 6
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    cpp_expression_err_line_break.pcpp
      a line break in a plain cpp("...") (PR0046)
    cpp_expression_err_prefix.pcpp
      cpp(...) takes no prefixed string (PR0009)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe cpp_expression;

#include <cstdlib>
#include <cstring>

begin
  println("abs {}", cpp("std::abs(-5)"));
  println("raw {}", cpp(R"(std::strlen("abc"))"));
  println("lines {}", cpp(R"(1 +
    2 +
    3)"));
end.
